  "rule": "the git-ignored inputs a clone lacks, from committed records only.  Per body: the two round-two model files plant.model_files names, <case>/models/<id>.xml with the candidate record's xml_sha256 (which must carry the plan's prefix, designlab.stage1.SHA256_PREFIX) and <id>.json with the sha256 a committed inputs list holds (bundle.INPUT_LISTS); where no committed record holds a file's sha256 the manifest holds the file's own and provenance.hash_sources lists none for it.  Per set and body: the files of the set's latest freeze manifest (set.json freezes[-1].manifest: refs/<name>.npz for a walk, transitions/<name>.npz for a move, with the freeze's sha256, which the entry in refs.json or transitions.json must hold too); never a look-format twin, never a file the freeze does not list.  A file that is missing or has another sha256 is refused; nothing is rebuilt.  Parts: models-<body>.tar; <set>-<body>-<i>.tar, i from 1, the set's files in sorted order, a new part when the next file would take the tar file past part_mb x 1,000,000 bytes.  Tar rules: USTAR, members sorted by name, each named by its path relative to the study, mtime 0, uid and gid 0, empty user and group names, mode 0644, no compression.  content_sha256 is s2io.sha256_json(content): the content block alone; provenance is outside it and nothing is added to content after the build",
